Z||000000||fiero56||12-03-1999||07:11 PM||||Another angry face from Andrew(Drew)(fiero56). I have had everything back together on my car since Tuesday.  The only thing keeping me from driving this thing is the passenger side axle will not seat.  It needs to go another half an inch to fully seat.  The drivers side went in perfectly.  Whats different with the passenger side.  I've been tapping, tugging, pulling, etc. Nothing works at getting it back in.  Is there some magic trick to doing this? I know some of you guys have pulled and reinstalled these, whats the trick?||||reg||8
Z||000001||theogre||12-03-1999||07:27 PM||||pull it out and check inside the tranny to make sure something isn't in there that doesn't belong.<P>make sure the tranny is locked in gear/park push and turn at the same time till the splines drop.<P>to get more control pushing it in, put a plastic or aluminum pipe over the outboard end. If you use steel pipe you MUST wrap the area the seal runs on in tape. Electricians or masking tape are best. with a 2-3 foot pipe you'll be able to line up the thing better so you can push straight without the outer end rocking on you.<P><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-03-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||12-03-1999||09:04 PM||||Ogre,<BR>You are THE MAN!<BR>I went outside, put the Fiero in gear, twisted the axle, and it popped in place in about 2 seconds.  I'm so mad at myself I'm ready to kick my own a$$. Thanks for the fast reply.  I will NEVER forget how to put in axles in a Fiero due to this mistake.  Hey everyone, big applause for Ogre! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
